WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.420
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.210
Get up.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:08.600
Who is it?

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.060
Three.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.060
Think of three things.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.370
Three things to live.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.240
Three things to go home.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.070
Three things to defeat the enemy.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.510
By thinking, you can still live.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.640
That's right.  Three.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.610
Respond, Cyberses!

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.080
Appear, Link 4!

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.320
Firewall Dragon!

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.360
The real fight is only getting started!

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.750
I run Across the universe

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.920
At the speed of light

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.790
Begin Loading

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:16.520
Open the door of dreams

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.090
VRAINS spreads

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.200
Believe in myself

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.730
VRAINS continues

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:32.040
The circuit draws the future

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.110
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.710
Access!

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.410
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.020
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.320
Link with my soul

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.090
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.820
Now Win the Race

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.660
Connected world

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.160
No matter when

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:58.530
Nothing is impossible

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:02.670
Strive for hope

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.240
And ride the wind!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.070
Firewall Dragon's effect!

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:38.070
For every monster that's 
linked to this card...

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:42.510
...a monster in the field or graveyard 
returns to its owner's hand.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.050
One monster is linked to Firewall.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.130
Emergency Escape!

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:52.450
I see.  That's a powerful effect.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.490
But monster effects can't 
target Borreload Dragon.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.430
Aww really?  That's the 
monster I want to get rid of!

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.030
I return Magnarokket Dragon to your hand.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.920
But Magnarokket's effect now activates!

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:14.160
When a Link Monster's effect 
targets it, I can destroy it.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.640
Then I send one monster on 
the field to the graveyard.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.720
I send Firewall to the graveyard!

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.970
Magnarokket's effect removes monsters.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.310
Hey!  If you lose Firewall...

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.120
I know!

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:33.360
I banish Cynet Refresh from my 
graveyard to activate its effect!

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:39.200
Card effects can't affect my 
Cyberse Link Monster this turn.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.850
You prevented Firewall's destruction.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:48.310
But I activate Magnarokket's other effect!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.800
When a battle or an effect destroys 
it, at the end of the turn...

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.750
...I Special Summon a different 
Rokket from my deck.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.720
I end my turn.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:02.950
Phew!  He finally ended his turn.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:08.740
Playmaker managed to destroy Fire 
Prison, but he's in bad shape.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.600
The next turn will be the decider.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.500
Playmaker...

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.010
Yusaku...

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.480
Revolver is undamaged, 
while we only have 600 LP.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.690
And no cards in our hand!

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.630
Everything will depend on this draw.

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:36.490
I've done everything I can 
in order to battle him.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.460
And built a deck to defeat him.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.200
For this one moment, I 
know my deck will respond.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.120
This draw is my destiny draw!

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.640
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.280
Yes!  This card will do!

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:02.510
From my hand, I activate the 
Continuous Spell, Battle Buffer!

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.720
As long as Encode and Firewall 
are linked to each other...

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:12.460
...Anesthrokket Dragon and Magnarokket 
Dragon's effects are sealed!

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:15.930
All right!

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:20.350
Now they can't become Borreload's bullets!

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.400
Let's go, Playmaker!

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:24.650
Battle!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.610
Firewall Dragon attacks Borreload Dragon!

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:34.850
You're attacking Borreload Dragon even 
though Firewall Dragon has lower ATK?

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:38.080
Encode Talker's effect!

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:44.490
Monsters linked to it aren't destroyed 
in battle nor take damage!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.130
What are you thinking?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.290
It means our strategy isn't over yet!

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.660
Go, Firewall Dragon!

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.100
Tempest Attack!

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.510
Encode's additional effect activates!

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:07.980
Firewall gains ATK equal to Borreload's ATK!

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:12.500
Is there any point raising 
Firewall's ATK after it attacked?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.000
There is!

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.960
The Continuous Spell Battle Buffer's effect!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.690
I place one Battle Buffer 
Counter on this card.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:27.930
Cyberse Link Monsters on my 
field gain 700 ATK per Counter!

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.400
Encode Talker now has more 
ATK than Borreload Dragon!

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.370
I see.  That's what you were going for.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.740
Go, Encode Talker!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.400
Attack Borreload Dragon!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.760
Final Encode!

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:46.350
Borreload Dragon's effect!

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:47.950
Anti Enemy Varrett!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:53.960
Once per turn, one monster 
loses 500 ATK and DEF.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.960
This effect can activate during your turn.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.350
And you can't activate a 
card to counter this effect.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:01.540
No way!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.810
Naturally, I'm reducing Encode Talker's ATK!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.780
Strike back, Borreload!

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:21.260
Encode Talker was destroyed!

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.960
But now, Battle Buffer's effect!

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.930
I place one Battle Buffer Counter.

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.840
Firewall's ATK increases again!

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.480
But your monsters aren't 
linked to each other anymore.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.970
So Battle Buffer can't seal away effects.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:45.380
Anesthrokket Dragon and Magnarokket 
Dragon's effects return.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.360
Playmaker has no monsters 
left that can attack.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:55.350
If Revolver uses Magnarokket's effect 
to remove Firewall next turn...

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:59.760
...Playmaker has no way 
to stop Revolver's attack.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.740
It seems this match is over.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.380
You can't attack anymore this turn.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.650
Are you sure about that?

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.330
What?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.820
You're going for it?

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:16.510
Since Borreload's effect is now over, I 
don't have to worry about Magnarokket's effect.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.160
This is my only chance to defeat him!

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.450
Don't mess up!

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:22.770
You don't need to tell me!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.050
Here I go!

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:29.120
I banish Recoded Alive from my 
graveyard to activate its effect!

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:30.990
A trap from the graveyard?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.890
Resurrect, Decode Talker!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:43.070
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for 
every monster that's linked to it!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:48.740
Your Borreload is linked to Decode Talker!

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.970
Power Integration!

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:55.610
There's still more!

00:08:55.610 --> 00:09:02.190
Due to the Field Spell Cynet Universe's 
effect, Decode Talker gains ATK!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.560
And the Continuous Spell 
Battle Buffer's effect!

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:11.530
Cyberse Link Monsters 
gain 700 ATK per Counter!

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:16.050
Decode Talker gains 1400 ATK!

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.000
Good!  It'll work this time!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.240
Go, Decode Talker!

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.970
Attack Borreload!

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:24.220
Decode End!

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.580
I activate the trap, Borrel Refrigeration!

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:35.290
By tributing Anesthrokket, I 
equip this card on Borreload.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:39.820
Borreload can now select 
one monster on my field.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:43.760
That monster can't be destroyed 
in battle or by effects.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.200
I select Magnarokket, of course!

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.580
Magnarokket's effect!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:55.770
When a Link Monster's effect 
targets it, I can destroy it.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:59.000
Then I send one monster on 
the field to the graveyard!

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.150
I send Decode Talker to the graveyard!

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.760
It's really over this time, Playmaker.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:15.520
Only Firewall Dragon remains on your field.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:19.760
It's powered up, but it 
already finished attacking.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.870
You have no cards in your 
hand and only 400 LP.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:26.870
You'll lose on my next turn!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:29.240
No, I won't lose.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:33.350
I have three reasons why I must defeat you!

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:40.320
#1: I'll defeat you and uncover the 
truth about what happened ten years ago!

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:45.920
#2: I'll regain the time that I lost!

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:50.530
#3: I'll save my friend who saved me!

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:54.120
Ten years ago...  Three things...

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:57.770
You're the one from that 
incident ten years ago?

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:02.870
That's right.  I'm that emissary of revenge!

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.950
Incident ten years ago?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.920
What's he talking about?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:16.890
It can't be...

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.070
Ten years ago...

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:23.300
If that's true, fate is scary.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.330
You're a fool, Playmaker.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.010
To help SOL Technologies 
without knowing the truth!

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.740
SOL Technologies?

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:40.240
Oh my.  The incident ten years ago...

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.120
SOL Technologies...

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:46.080
Did I overhear something very interesting?

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:50.200
There's only one thing I must do.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:55.430
I'll crush the Knights of 
Hanoi and learn everything!

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.770
I activate Parallel Port Armor's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:07.000
I can activate it by banishing this card 
and two Link Monsters from my graveyard!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:12.480
My Link Monster can battle twice this turn!

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:16.430
What?  Firewall can attack again?

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:18.220
Go, Playmaker!

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:21.190
Firewall attacks!

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:22.920
Tempest Attack!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:28.590
Borreload can't be destroyed, 
but you take damage!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.620
Playmaker won!

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:41.190
All right!  You did it, Yusaku!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.540
With this...

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:53.180
As promised, I'll take 
the information you have!

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:56.120
I'll eat it up!

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:11.320
I'll eat up everything!

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.260
What?

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:18.310
Father!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:25.520
Interference from the outside.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.800
Ai!  Return!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.520
Damn!

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.460
Hey!  Trying to escape?

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.320
I keep my promises.

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:40.400
Take it!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.720
It's the removal program.

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.500
Playmaker!

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:48.740
The wind didn't blow for me today.

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:54.980
But as long as you have that AI, 
this duel was the only the start.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.450
We will meet again.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:06.160
Aww, he escaped!  We were so close!

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:07.450
Revolver...

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.290
Playmaker!

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.320
This is the removal program.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.860
With this, she'll be...

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.300
Where's Aoi?

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.350
Seems she was able to log out.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:51.470
That means...

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.710
You should go to her.

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:56.770
Okay!

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:58.520
Playmaker!

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:02.910
Oh?

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.940
You're already leaving?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.080
How cool.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.350
Playmaker.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.470
Thank you.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:17.510
Isomaki?

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:20.260
Why are you here?

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:22.300
I received an anonymous tip.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.220
Please get in.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.270
I'll take you to the hospital.

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.680
Must be Emma.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:30.680
Thanks.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.450
Are you okay?

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:41.720
Yeah.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:45.690
How's Aoi Zaizen?

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.640
Aoi!

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.330
Aoi!

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:57.840
Aoi!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:03.570
Brother...

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:05.710
Aoi!

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:09.790
Brother, I'm sorry.

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.790
It's fine.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:14.050
You don't have to say anything.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:15.670
Just rest.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.260
Thank goodness.

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.960
Truly.

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.670
She's okay.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:35.140
Huh?

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:38.970
He fell asleep.  How lazy.

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:43.380
Heroes need rest too.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:46.140
You think he's a hero?

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:50.350
A hero is someone like me!  
Smart and wonderful and cool-

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.360
What are you doing?

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.670
I'm going to analyze the program you ate.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:59.780
What?  You're going to 
look at my private parts?

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.620
You're a pervert.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:04.540
To tell you the truth, 
I don't need to do this.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.670
If you tell me what program you ate.

00:17:07.140 --> 00:17:12.000
It's...  Umm...  It's...

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.000
It was pointless to ask.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.010
You're no fun.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.990
Let your guard down?

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:25.200
It's not like you.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:30.330
Or were you shaken when he 
talked about ten years ago?

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.340
I'm sorry, Father.

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:35.800
But next time, I promise!

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.600
It's fine.  Don't worry about it.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.510
I was able to get useful data from the duel.

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.480
But if we can't acquire that Ignis...

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.480
...I must proceed with the final plan.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.080
I'll being making preparations.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:52.980
Understood.

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.520
Three things...  That speech pattern...

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.530
Playmaker, are you...

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:10.500
Zaizen learned something he shouldn't have.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:15.700
It's dangerous to keep him 
in his current position.

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:18.740
Before he becomes too curious...

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.320
What about his successor?

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:24.000
I think Kitamura is qualified.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.500
He's ambitious.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:30.720
If we entice him with a promotion, 
he'll happily accept.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:33.230
He's so predictable.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:35.830
Those kinds of pieces are good pieces.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:45.100
It seems you don't know what Ignis is.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.110
I'll tell you before you lose.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:50.740
Ignis isn't a regular AI.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:57.860
Since long ago, there have been tests 
to create life within the network.

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:03.550
But only regular programs 
were able to be created.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:08.160
They lacked a certain something 
to be considered a life form.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.560
What do you mean?

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:12.690
I...

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:14.430
You're awake.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.400
I'm almost done analyzing Ai's data.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.390
Did you learn anything?

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:22.510
You're also curious about what Revolver said?

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:26.760
Ignis is AI with free will.

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:28.250
Free will?

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:32.120
No way!  A program can't have free will!

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:35.770
AI with free will...

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:38.830
Revolver said that free will equals life.

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.860
That means this thing is alive.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:46.360
That's why the Knights of 
Hanoi desperately want him.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.370
But how can you prove he's alive?

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:53.230
It's not like he has a beating heart.

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:55.690
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:58.110
We're discussing whether you're alive or not.

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:01.110
Oh, I get it now.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:07.120
So that's what Revolver was talking 
about while I was asleep.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.970
Of course I'm alive!

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:11.370
I can do this!

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.570
Prove it.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.280
You'll learn soon enough.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:17.770
What's this?

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.170
Is it image data?

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:23.570
This program is incomprehensible.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.950
It can't be entirely analyzed.

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:29.570
That's because-  Do you want me to tell you?

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:32.540
I've already finished analyzing it.

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.380
Don't be arrogant.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:36.910
Or I will disassemble your program.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:39.920
Now now.  Don't be impatient.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:43.420
I don't know if I should show it to humans...

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:47.440
But you're special.  You should thank me!

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.980
Ta daa!

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:18.050
How's this!  This is my true form!

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:22.010
I retrieved my body's program 
from the Knights of Hanoi!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:25.600
Well?  I'm cute and cool, right?

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.900
This is great!

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:28.780
I'm invincible and powerful!

00:21:28.780 --> 00:21:29.720
This is it?

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.310
You don't remember anything else?

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:41.550
No.  The program I ate 
only contained my body.

00:21:43.170 --> 00:21:45.660
Recheck and see if we overlooked anything.

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:47.260
Yeah.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:48.520
Hey hey hey!

00:21:48.520 --> 00:21:50.060
Wait a second!

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:52.770
No reaction after seeing this body?

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.350
Like surprise?  Or happy for me?

00:21:56.350 --> 00:22:02.200
C'mon!  Look at me more!

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:27.380
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:30.920
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.340 --> 00:22:34.520
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:38.560
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.480 --> 00:22:42.480
Try It over and over

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:50.640
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:57.580
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.140
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.820
In these isolated times

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:03.550
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.810 --> 00:23:05.320
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.580 --> 00:23:08.750
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:12.320
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.520 --> 00:23:16.290
The miracles we create

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:18.500
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:22.340
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.940
One battle regarding LINK VRAINS has ended.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.450
But this is nothing more than a waypoint.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:45.520
"AI with free will."

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:48.980
These words weigh heavily on Yusaku.

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:53.880
The rivalry of fate has only begun, 
not knowing when it will end.

00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:58.330
What will happen when AI has free will?

00:23:58.530 --> 00:24:02.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Battle Record

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.530
Into the VRAINS!
